     "img": "l4_streaming",
     "text": "If you haven’t heard of “Gulf Coast,” you probably will soon. The new eight-episode series, now streaming on Hulu, follows Maria, a nurse who moves from Ohio to a small town near Sarasota after her divorce. She expects quiet beaches and early retirement-style living. Instead, she finds a hurricane, a mystery and a neighbor who knows far too much about everyone.\n\nThe first episode is slow. I almost gave up after twenty minutes, and some viewers online say the same thing. But stick with it: by episode three, the show finds its rhythm, and by episode five, I was completely hooked. I binge-watched the last four episodes in one night, which I do not recommend if you have work the next morning.\n\nThe cast is the real reason to watch. The actress who plays Maria is funny without trying too hard, and her relationship with her teenage son feels honest. The supporting characters, especially the local fishing-boat captain, steal almost every scene.\n\nThe show also gets Florida right. The humidity, the pop-up storms, the strip malls and the beautiful sunsets are all there. Locals will laugh at the jokes about tourists driving too slowly and the endless debate about the “best” beach.\n\nIt’s not perfect. The plot has a few holes, and one storyline about a stolen boat goes nowhere. Some of the dialogue is a little cheesy. Still, it’s one of the most enjoyable shows of the year.\n\nNo spoilers here, but I will say this: the season ends on a cliffhanger, and a second season has not been confirmed yet. Watch at your own risk.\n\nRating: 4 out of 5 stars.",
